  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116124",
      "title": "Understanding How Angular Performs Change Detection",
      "lectureOrder": 195,
      "videoOrder": 187,
      "sourceHash": "956773c6751001beaa86ac8b7ce5aba15adf7b965b13dfc3ce797913c137fb3a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.84,
          "end": 3.09,
          "en": "So how does Angular's",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.09,
          "end": 6.78,
          "en": "change detection mechanism work by default?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.78,
          "end": 10.11,
          "en": "Well, by default, you have your component tree",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.11,
          "end": 13.59,
          "en": "and Angular wraps that entire tree.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.59,
          "end": 16.59,
          "en": "In the end, it wraps your entire application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.59,
          "end": 19.83,
          "en": "with a so-called zone, which is a feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.83,
          "end": 24.12,
          "en": "that's provided by Zone.js, an extra library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.12,
          "end": 26.76,
          "en": "that's maintained by the Angular team",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.76,
          "end": 29.07,
          "en": "and that's heavily used by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.07,
          "end": 31.41,
          "en": "since it's that Zone.js library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.41,
          "end": 34.2,
          "en": "and that zone wrapper that's being set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.2,
          "end": 38.22,
          "en": "that informs Angular about potential events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.22,
          "end": 42.78,
          "en": "that are going on on the page that could potentially lead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.78,
          "end": 46.953,
          "en": "to changes that should be reflected on the screen therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.09,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "For example, if a user clicks a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 51.87,
          "en": "Angular gets notified about that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.87,
          "end": 55.41,
          "en": "and then it's change detection process starts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.41,
          "end": 59.22,
          "en": "and visits all components in the entire application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.22,
          "end": 61.53,
          "en": "no matter where that click occurred.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.53,
          "end": 65.01,
          "en": "It visits all components in the entire application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.01,
          "end": 67.59,
          "en": "and takes a look at all the templates there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.59,
          "end": 69.75,
          "en": "and all the template bindings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.75,
          "end": 73.62,
          "en": "so all the uses of property binding and string interpolation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.62,
          "end": 77.34,
          "en": "and so on and Angular checks whether",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.34,
          "end": 81.3,
          "en": "that binding now produces a new value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.3,
          "end": 84,
          "en": "if it produces a value that's different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84,
          "end": 85.98,
          "en": "from what was visible before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.98,
          "end": 89.73,
          "en": "And if that's the case, Angular updates the real DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.73,
          "end": 92.00999999999999,
          "en": "with that new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.00999999999999,
          "end": 94.56,
          "en": "That's how change detection works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.56,
          "end": 97.983,
          "en": "by default in Angular applications.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99,
          "end": 102.18,
          "en": "And that's why in this application, if we reload it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.18,
          "end": 105.15,
          "en": "and clear this log, if I click this one button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.15,
          "end": 109.53999999999999,
          "en": "this increment button here, we get lots of log messages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.49000000000001,
          "end": 112.89,
          "en": "because I essentially get one log message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.89,
          "end": 116.16,
          "en": "from every component because all components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.16,
          "end": 118.53,
          "en": "and their templates are revisited.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.53,
          "end": 120.84,
          "en": "And as I mentioned, all the template bindings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.84,
          "end": 123,
          "en": "are reevaluated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123,
          "end": 126.72,
          "en": "and that's why I added this debugOutput getter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.72,
          "end": 130.14,
          "en": "to all my components so that in the templates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 130.14,
          "end": 131.79,
          "en": "of those components, I can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.79,
          "end": 135.15,
          "en": "that getter property, debugOutput,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.15,
          "end": 138.15,
          "en": "which will be reevaluated since it's used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.15,
          "end": 140.04,
          "en": "with string interpolation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.04,
          "end": 143.01,
          "en": "And therefore, I'm using a template binding feature here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.01,
          "end": 145.62,
          "en": "And as I just explained, Angular visits",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.62,
          "end": 148.07999999999998,
          "en": "and checks all template bindings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.07999999999998,
          "end": 151.77,
          "en": "when its change detection process runs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 151.77,
          "end": 154.23,
          "en": "So therefore, the getter function gets executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.23,
          "end": 157.38,
          "en": "whenever Angular evaluates that template binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.38,
          "end": 160.62,
          "en": "And therefore, I can log that message here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.62,
          "end": 161.61,
          "en": "so that in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.61,
          "end": 165.9,
          "en": "I get one log message per evaluated template binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.9,
          "end": 169.95,
          "en": "Though I'm, of course, only logging template binding checks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.95,
          "end": 174.95,
          "en": "for this debugOutput property, not for any other bindings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 175.07999999999998,
          "end": 177.54,
          "en": "but still, we can see that we got a lot of logs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.54,
          "end": 179.91,
          "en": "and most importantly, we can see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.91,
          "end": 183.75,
          "en": "that all components are visited and checked,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.75,
          "end": 187.32,
          "en": "even components that have nothing to do with the counter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.32,
          "end": 190.5,
          "en": "because keep in mind, I'm just changing the counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 190.5,
          "end": 194.643,
          "en": "Nonetheless, a lot of other components are visited as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.63,
          "end": 199.02,
          "en": "Now, this might sound like a big problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.02,
          "end": 201.78,
          "en": "and it theoretically could be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 201.78,
          "end": 205.23,
          "en": "if you're doing some performance-intensive work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 205.23,
          "end": 207.15,
          "en": "in your template bindings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 207.15,
          "end": 210.27,
          "en": "but that is therefore also something you should avoid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.27,
          "end": 212.52,
          "en": "as an Angular developer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.52,
          "end": 214.77,
          "en": "You should not have getters",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 214.77,
          "end": 218.57999999999998,
          "en": "that perform super complex tasks, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 218.57999999999998,
          "end": 221.16,
          "en": "because they get executed a lot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.16,
          "end": 224.67000000000002,
          "en": "So if you're doing something performance wise expensive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 224.67000000000002,
          "end": 226.86,
          "en": "in there, that's bad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.86,
          "end": 230.67000000000002,
          "en": "If you adhere to that rule, it's actually no problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230.67000000000002,
          "end": 233.43,
          "en": "or at least not necessarily a problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 233.43,
          "end": 236.07,
          "en": "that Angular performs a lot of checks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.07,
          "end": 237.96,
          "en": "because Angular is built",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 237.96,
          "end": 241.17,
          "en": "such that it does that very efficiently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 241.17,
          "end": 244.77,
          "en": "Nonetheless, you will learn later that you can get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 244.77,
          "end": 246,
          "en": "of some of these checks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 246,
          "end": 250.023,
          "en": "and that you can put some optimizations into place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 251.01,
          "end": 254.16,
          "en": "Before we do that though, and before we take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 254.16,
          "end": 257.61,
          "en": "at alternative change detection strategies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 257.61,
          "end": 259.92,
          "en": "I wanna clarify something else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 259.92,
          "end": 263.16,
          "en": "because if you take a closer look at the log output here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 263.16,
          "end": 264.6,
          "en": "you might notice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 264.6,
          "end": 268.773,
          "en": "that it's actually the same log being output twice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 269.67,
          "end": 273.36,
          "en": "All these components are visited twice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 273.36,
          "end": 275.4,
          "en": "and that's a bit weird",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 275.4,
          "end": 279.18,
          "en": "because one check makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 279.18,
          "end": 282.843,
          "en": "but why does Angular perform two checks here?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
